---
description: Adapter for ship-related code and asset integration
globs:
  - "Source/**/*Ship*"
  - "Content/Ship/**"
  - "Content/Ships/**"
  - "docs/specs/systems/ship-system/**"
  - "docs/specs/assets/ships/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

For ship-related work, read in order:

- `spec-manifest.yaml`
- `Docs/governance/source-of-truth.md`
- `docs/specs/systems/ship-system/ship-system.md`
- `Docs/specs/assets/ships/production-rules.md`
- `docs/specs/systems/ship-system/ship-system.yaml`
- `docs/specs/systems/ship-system/ship-program.md`
- `Docs/specs/assets/ships/index.yaml`
- the target ship's `design.md`
- the target ship's bound/specified material card when visual production is involved
- the target ship's `integration.yaml`

For visual work, apply `Docs/specs/assets/ships/production-rules.md` before loading any visual master. In clean-slate “重新/重出” work, do not use the previous concept/master image as generation input. For direct image editing, use the user-designated image as the edit base.

Do not trigger image production merely because the final asset pipeline is visual; analyze the user's text first and only generate when the user explicitly requests a visual deliverable.

`.cursor/rules/ship-system.mdc` is an adapter entry only. Canonical facts are under `Docs/specs` / `docs/specs`; do not maintain a second conflicting rule set here.
